CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ packs of a qualified type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
too many template arguments
--
With concepts enabled (C++20, or the MSVC STL in Visual Studio mode) a
template parameter beginning with a qualified name is parsed by the
concept-aware path; it moved the ellipsis of a pointer declarator to the
declarator-id but not that of a plain one, so `N::size_type... I' was a
single parameter.
